## Documented lessons

The Windows script-encoding rules repeated in `docs/DEPLOY.md` (`.cmd`/`.bat` must be
ASCII-only because cmd.exe decodes them with the system ANSI code page; a `.ps1` containing
non-ASCII must carry a UTF-8 BOM because PowerShell 5.1 otherwise decodes it as ANSI) were
learned the hard way and are recorded here so nobody has to rediscover them.
